# TypeScript backend standards

## Imports & structure

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — imports at top; route → service → cache/db
import { Router, Request, Response } from 'express';
import * as tripService from '../services/tripService';
import * as driverContextService from '../services/driverContextService';

// ❌ BAD — dynamic import inside handler unless breaking circular dep
router.get('/x', async (req, res) => {
  const { get } = await import('../services/tripService');
});
```

## Control flow — always use blocks

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
if (!trip) {
  return res.status(404).json({ detail: 'Trip not found' });
}

// ❌ BAD — single-line if without braces (easy to break on edit)
if (!trip) return res.status(404).json({ detail: 'Trip not found' });
```

Use **early return** in routes. Keep handlers thin — delegate to `services/`.

## Service layer

New work lives in `services/<name>/` (folder). Canonical adapters: `maps/`, `notify/`. Flat `*Service.ts` files are legacy — convert when that file is next edited. Full rules: `.cursor/rules/service-layer.mdc`.

| Service | Responsibility |
|---------|----------------|
| `tripService.ts` | DynamoDB CRUD (legacy flat file) |
| `driverContextService.ts` | Build/cache driver context |
| `earningsService.ts` | Fare + earnings calculations |
| `maps/` | Route/matrix adapters (Goong / Google) |
| `notify/` | Local WS vs Lambda push |
| `routes/*.ts` | HTTP only — validate, call service, map response |

- Export functions from the package façade. Inject collaborators as args; do not add a DI container.
- Invalidate cache in routes after writes: `invalidateTripParties()`

## Types

- Extend `Trip` interface for new fields — avoid `(trip as Record<string, unknown>)`
- Shared constants at module top: `UPCOMING`, `ACTIVE` status sets
